# Needs the selection build: flutter build apk --debug --dart-define=PROBE_AGENT=true --dart-define=PROBE_FIXTURE_WIDGETS=selection (see README).
# What each test shows is also in docs/compat/MATRIX.md: a matrix cell is set only from a test that ran.

before each test
  restart the app
  # the last element of the screen: right after a restart the agent can answer while the screen is still being built (issue #793)
  wait until #wf_cupertino_switch_state appears

# `don't see "..." is checked` also passes when the element is absent; the `see "..." is checked` steps of the same tests are its positive twins.
test "a checkbox turns on and off"
  see "Terms: off"
  don't see "Accept terms" is checked
  toggle "Accept terms"
  see "Terms: on"
  see "Accept terms" is checked
  toggle "Accept terms"
  see "Terms: off"
  don't see "Accept terms" is checked

test "a switch turns on"
  see "Notifications: off"
  toggle "Notifications"
  see "Notifications: on"
  see "Notifications" is checked

# `is checked` on a radio needs a probe_agent that reads the group value of a RadioGroup (docs/compat/MATRIX.md): an older agent fails the `is checked` steps.
test "a radio group takes one choice at a time"
  see "Size: small"
  tap "Medium"
  see "Size: medium"
  see "Medium" is checked
  don't see "Small" is checked
  tap "Large"
  see "Size: large"
  see "Large" is checked
  don't see "Medium" is checked

test "a swipe across a slider moves its value"
  see "Volume: 50"
  swipe right on #wf_slider
  see "Volume" matching "Volume: (5[1-9]|[6-9][0-9]|100)"

test "a Cupertino switch turns on"
  see "Cupertino switch: off"
  toggle #wf_cupertino_switch
  see "Cupertino switch: on"
